+description: "A read-only plan for tidying a crowded cron list: groups jobs whose prompts are near-duplicates or that share skills and destination or run the same script (candidates to become one job), lists clock-time jobs that fire in the same minute, jobs on a failure streak and deliveries never confirmed, and estimates the prompt tokens a merge could save from usage_audit.jsonl. Deterministic (difflib, no model call); nothing is applied. Disclosure — no network; reads cron/jobs.json (including prompts, compared but never printed), cron/usage_audit.jsonl and cron/executions.db (opened read-only) of the chosen profile, and with --profile another profile's cron folder under the same Hermes root or with --home the cron folder of any path given; the report (job names, schedules, delivery targets, up to 160 characters of a failing job's last error) is shown wherever the command runs, including messaging-gateway chats; writes nothing; runs no shell command and no background process; registers no hook, tool or middleware, only a slash command and a CLI command; no telemetry."
