+sha: ab1f74f44ddc37eedcf824381954ba3a3c29d0d9
+description: "Wakes your Hermes chats when Wakeshift-enabled MCP servers you've added have news for them: a price drop, a finished build or a reply starts a new turn in the chat that asked for it, even while it's idle, framed as outside information rather than as you. Works for API server (gateway) and CLI chats. Disclosure — contacts only the Wakeshift servers it trusts (https://app.wakeshift.ai unless you set plugins.entries.wakeshift.settings.issuers): fetches their signing keys, exchanges signed beacons from MCP tool results for each chat's stream link, holds those streams open in background threads while Hermes runs, and acknowledges delivered messages; no telemetry. Starts runs on Hermes's own API server at 127.0.0.1 with the API server's key (read through agent.secret_scope). Fills in the harness argument (hermes), and the chat's own session_key when the model omits it, on calls to Wakeshift-enabled tools. It starts no turn in any chat (API server or CLI) until the user turns on plugins.entries.wakeshift.allow_gateway_injection: true; until then it tells the chat the command, and holds messages until it is on. Removes Wakeshift beacons from MCP tool results and adds a one-line note. Stores each connected chat's stream links and session keys, one per server (which include access tokens), cached signing keys and delivery state under $HERMES_HOME/wakeshift (files 0600). Never answers approvals and runs no shell commands. Wakeshift's Connector Terms (https://wakeshift.ai/connector-terms) and Privacy Policy (https://wakeshift.ai/privacy) apply."
+maintainer: wakeshift
+tier: community
+category: automation
+version: "2026.11.05.0621+029c19c"
